 "path_rule": "corrected rule (sponsor, 2026-11-25 10:04 EST): flow = presynaptic activation times weight over the fixed 200-problem validation set; a weight synapse passes iff its flow std is at least half the largest flow std among the weight synapses feeding the same node; the main path is the passing synapses on a connected entry-to-exit route (routes may step through the residual and attention/logit conduits, which are structural connectors, not competitors). The generalised machinery was validated against stitch #2: run on species 8 and 9 it reproduces the recorded path sets exactly (13 and 26 synapses).",
 "attn_scale": {
  "value": 0.7071067811865475,
  "why": "the engine's initial-arch scale at d=2 (arch.attn_scale of be.initial_arch(cfg, 2)). Both Franks were built and evolved under this value for every block's attention and the decoder logits; the two-Franks network keeps it so every copied weight retains the scale it was built/evolved under. It is used for all three blocks' attention and the decoder logits, as in every earlier build."
 },
 "layout": "stream width 8: Frank #1's territory on coordinates 0-3, Frank #2's on 4-7. Two-Franks block 1 carries Frank #1's block-1 path and Frank #2's block-1 path side by side; block 2 carries each Frank's block-2 path in the same way (both Franks have two blocks, so each Frank's extracted branch material is placed in its original block order, block 1 then block 2, inside its own territory). Block 3 is the joining block, all filler.",
 "joining_ffn_width_reading": "the joining block's FFN width = the sum of the two Franks' FFN path widths, each Frank's width counted in the block that feeds the joining block on that side (each Frank's block 2: Frank #1 4 units, Frank #2 4 units) = 8, which equals the two-Franks block-2 FFN width \u2014 the same relation as stitches #2/#4 and the Squared build, where the joining FFN width equalled the preceding block's FFN width.",
